-- title:
--   Gradient is invariant under equality of functions
-- statement:
--   If two functions $f, g : E \to \mathbb{R}$ are equal as functions, then their gradients agree everywhere: for every $z \in E$,
--   $$\nabla f(z) = \nabla g(z).$$
--   This is the congruence rule that lets subsequent gradient computations replace a function by an equal one.
